        "mission_intent": "We need a comprehensive collection plan stood up to monitor China's commercial space sector trajectory and its potential dual-use implications for PLA space-based ISR and satcom capabilities, with particular emphasis on identifying which international partners are being courted for Beijing's lunar research station initiative as an alternative to the Artemis Accords framework. The plan should leverage all available open-source, SIGINT, and GEOINT capabilities to map the full commercial-military nexus in China's space enterprise, including tracking launch cadence, orbital deployments, ground infrastructure expansion, and any technology transfer arrangements with partner nations. We want this to be an enduring collection effort with quarterly deliverables, but I need the initial baseline assessment delivered within two weeks that covers the entirety of China's space modernization trajectory through 2030 across all technology sub-domains\u2014crewed spaceflight, PNT constellations, commercial launch providers, ISR architecture, and counterspace programs. The assessment should reflect best-efforts analytic confidence levels throughout, and the team should coordinate with NRO and DIA equities to avoid duplication while ensuring no seams in coverage of emerging commercial entities that may serve as PLA procurement fronts.",
